## Lyric Storage & Schema

Lyrics are stored in the database `lyrics` table supporting multiple variants per track (`original`, `romanized`, `translated`).

---

## Content Sanitization Pipeline (`cleanGeniusContent`)

Raw lyrics scraped from external sources (e.g. Genius, Musixmatch, Last.fm) pass through a 8-stage cleaning pipeline before parsing:

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    Raw["Raw Scraped Lyrics"] --> HTML["1. Strip HTML tags (<div/>, <img/>)"]
    HTML --> ReadMore["2. Remove 'Read More' blocks"]
    ReadMore --> Contributors["3. Strip 'X Contributors' & 'Translations' headers"]
    Contributors --> Headers["4. Remove generic 'Lyrics' headers"]
    Headers --> Sections["5. Strip Section Labels ([Verse 1], [Chorus])"]
    Sections --> Title["6. Deduplicate duplicate song titles at top"]
    Title --> Trim["7. Normalize CRLF / LF line endings"]
    Trim --> Clean["8. Pure Lyric Lines Array"]
```

---

## LRC Parsing & Timestamp Calculation (`parseLRC`)

Raw LRC strings with time tags (e.g. `[01:23.45] Line text`) are parsed by `lyric-parser.service.ts` into normalized millisecond objects:

1. **Timestamp Extraction**: Matched via regex `\[(\d+):(\d+)(?:\.(\d+))?\]`.
2. **Millisecond Normalization**: Minutes (`m`), seconds (`s`), and fractional milliseconds (`ms`) are converted to absolute milliseconds (`t`):
   ```text
   t = (m * 60 + s) * 1000 + ms
   ```
3. **Title Token Highlighting**: Words matching the song title are tokenized and flagged (`highlight: true`) for client UI animations.
4. **Chronological Sorting**: Lines are sorted in ascending order by timestamp (`a.t - b.t`).

---

## Proportional Timing Fallback Algorithm

When lyrics exist only as **plain text** without LRC timestamps, `lament-api` dynamically calculates estimated timestamps based on the total track duration (`durationMs`):

```text
step = durationMs / (plainLines.length + 1)
timestamp[i] = floor(step * (i + 1))
```

### Fallback Calculation Example:
For a 180-second track (180,000 ms) with 9 plain lyric lines:
- `step` = `180,000 / (9 + 1) = 18,000 ms` (18 seconds per line).
- Line 1 $\to$ 18,000 ms, Line 2 $\to$ 36,000 ms, Line 3 $\to$ 54,000 ms, etc.

> [!TIP]
> This proportional timing algorithm guarantees that even unsynced plain text lyrics trigger progressive scrolling and line highlighting in web and mobile karaoke views.

---

## Variant Resolution & Fallback Logic

When a client queries `GET /lyrics/:id?variant=romanized`:

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    Request["GET /lyrics/:id?variant=romanized"] --> CheckCache{"Cache Hit in Redis/LRU?"}
    CheckCache -- Yes --> ReturnCache["Return Cached JSON"]
    CheckCache -- No --> DB["Query DB for track_id"]
    DB --> MatchVariant{"Match Requested Variant?"}
    MatchVariant -- Found --> Parse["Parse LRC & Proportional Timing"]
    MatchVariant -- Not Found --> FallbackOriginal{"Variant 'original' Exists?"}
    FallbackOriginal -- Yes --> Parse
    FallbackOriginal -- No --> Error404["Return 404 No Lyrics Found"]
    Parse --> SaveCache["Cache Response (86,400s)"]
    SaveCache --> ReturnJSON["Return JSON Response"]
```
